Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 08:56:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] LvglDisplayEngineDxe: Title an information popup with
 only OK as such

A popup of EFI_HII_POPUP_PROTOCOL with the information style is titled
"Confirm", which fits a question with Yes and No, not a message with just
OK, such as a driver reporting that a password was set. Title the latter
"Information".

Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 LvglDisplayEngineDxe/LvglFormRenderer.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/LvglDisplayEngineDxe/LvglFormRenderer.c b/LvglDisplayEngineDxe/LvglFormRenderer.c
index ba24553..0f89438 100644
--- a/LvglDisplayEngineDxe/LvglFormRenderer.c
+++ b/LvglDisplayEngineDxe/LvglFormRenderer.c
@@ -6037,7 +6037,10 @@ LvglHiiCreatePopup (
       Title = "Warning";
       break;
     default:
-      Title = "Confirm";
+      //
+      // An information popup with just OK tells, it does not ask.
+      //
+      Title = (PopupType == EfiHiiPopupTypeOk) ? "Information" : "Confirm";
       break;
   }
 
